          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em quasicoherent sheaf of modules
            (often just “quasicoherent sheaf”, for short) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+of+modules"} sheaf of modules
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            that is
            %em
              locally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+module"} presentable
            in that it is locally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of a morphism of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+modules"} free modules
          %p
            For comparison, by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            is equivalently encoded in its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
            which is even locally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of vector bundles is too small to be closed under various natural operations like
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+images"} direct images
            and alike. In particular, it is not an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+category"} abelian category
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            of quasicoherent sheaves of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
          %p There are several different but equivalent ways to define and think of quasicoherent sheaves.
          %p
            A very concrete definition characterizes quasicoherent sheaves as those that are, while not locally free, locally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of a morphism of free module sheaves. This is the definition given in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#LocPres"} As locally presentable modules
          %p
            below. It makes very manifest how passing from vector bundles to quasicoherent sheaves adds in the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
          %p
            But it turns out that there is a more abstract, more
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+and+topos+theory"} sheaf theoretic
            reformulation of this definition: if we think of the underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            as a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"}> pre
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            (as motivated at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AsSheaves"}> As sheaves over Aff/X
              \.
          %p and in more details in the section
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AsSheavesII"}> Definition as sheaves over Aff
              \.
          %p
            The tensoring operation appearing here is that defining the pullback operations in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            that classifies the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to CRing
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC := (-)Mod : Ring \to Cat
            the functor that sends a ring to its category of modules, one finds that the category of quasicoherent sheaves on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space"} space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is simply the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC(X) := Hom(X,QC)
          %p
            in the corresponding 2-category of category-valued (pre)sheaves, i.e (pre)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"}> stack
            s. This is the perspective described in
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AsCocycles"} As hom objects
          %p
            below. By the equivalence between
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
            with the category of cartesian functors between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#AsFibHoms"} As cartesian morphisms of fibered categories
          %p
            This definition, finally, provides a powerful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
            on quasicoherent sheaves: all notions involved, sheaf, stack, morphism of stacks, have natural, immediate and well understood generalizations to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            = succeed "-sheaves" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#Higher"}> Higher quasicoherent sheaves
              \.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#LocPres As locally presentable modules
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,O_X)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+space"} ringed space
            or, more generally, a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+site"} ringed site
          %p
            A
            %strong
              quasicoherent sheaf of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi O
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
          %p
            This means: there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mrow
                      %mi α
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_\alpha\}_{\alpha\in A}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by open sets such that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            there exist
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_\alpha
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J_\alpha
            (not necessarily finite) and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact sequence
            of sheaves of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi I
                        %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi O
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi J
                        %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℰ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi α
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  O_X^{I_\alpha}|_{U_\alpha}
                  \\to
                  O_X^{J_\alpha}|_{U_\alpha}
                  \\to
                  \\mathcal{E}|_{U_\alpha}\to 0,
          %p
            This should be viewed as a
            %em local presentation
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi I
                    %mi α
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi J
                    %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_\alpha, J_\alpha
            can be chosen finite and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is of finite type then the quasicoherent sheaf is a
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} coherent sheaf
            = succeed "s;" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+scheme"} Noetherian scheme
          %p
            Replacing covers by open sets, by covers of a terminal object in a site, the definition extends to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ringed+site"} ringed site
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+stack"} algebraic stack
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0012061"} configuration schemes
            of V. Lunts, obtained by gluing along closed embeddings of schemes; simplicial schemes) and so on.
          %h3#AsSheaves
            As sheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
          %p
            There is an equivalent reformulation of the above in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+scheme"} affine scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+category"} over category
            whose objects are morphism (of
            = succeed "s)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A \to X
            and whose morphisms are commuting triangles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spec
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mi a
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Spec A &amp;&amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp;&amp; Spec B
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_a\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_b
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then: a quasicoherent sheaf on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, \mathcal{O}_X)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
            such that for each morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            as above the restriction morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N(f) : N(b) \to N(a)
          %p
            extends to an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N(b) \otimes_{f^*} A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} N(a)
          %p
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
          %p
            For a very explicit statement of this see for instance
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/arxiv/pdf/0910/0910.5130v1.pdf#page=13"} page 13
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
              ,
              %em Topological modular forms (aftern Hopkins, Miller, and Lurie)
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0910.5130"}> arXiv
              )
          %p See also a very precise and detailed treatment in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Orlov"}> Dmitri Orlov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quasi-coherent sheaves in commutative and non-commutative geometry
              = succeed ":3," do
                %strong 67
              %a{:href => "http://web.archive.org/web/20210506231653/http://www.mi-ras.ru/~orlov/papers/NST.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=57"} dvi
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=56"} ps
          %h3#AsSheavesII Direct definition for presheaves of sets on Aff
          %p Here is a more detailed way to say again what the above paragraph said.
          %p
            Let
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff = CRing^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod\to CRing^{op}
            where for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing
            the inverse image functor is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mo −
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^*=B\otimes_A - :{}_A Mod\to {}_B Mod
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo →
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing\to CRing
            can be interpreted as the presheaf of rings and is denoted by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            (the “structure sheaf”). An
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing
          %p
            A
            %strong
              quasicoherent sheaf of
              = succeed "-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a rule assigning to any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\in X(A)
            an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_\phi = M_{A,\phi}
            and to any morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to B
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing
            an isomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_{f,\phi}:f^*(M_\phi)\to M_{X(f)(\phi)}
            such that for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composable+pair"} composable pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi B
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi g
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\stackrel{f}\to B\stackrel{g}\to C
            and any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\in X(A)
            the cocycle condition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi fg
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\theta_{g\circ f,\phi}\circ \alpha_{fg} = \theta_{g,X(f)(\phi)}\circ g^*(\theta_{f,\phi})\colon g^* f^*(M_\phi)\to M_{X(g\circ f)(\phi)}
          %p
            holds, where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mi fg
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi g
                    %mo *
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{fg}:g^* f^*(M_\phi)\to (g\circ f)^*(M_\phi)
            is the canonical isomorphism which is part of the data of the (covariant) pseudofunctor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to {}_A Mod
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\mapsto f^*
          %p
            Notice that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi h
                    %mi C
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi h
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = h^C = h_{Spec C}
            is (co)representable presheaf, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi Pshv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Aff
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi CRing
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\in [A,X]_{Pshv(Aff)}=[C,A]_{CRing}
            is the same as a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi op
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi^{op}:C\to A
            of rings; restricting the quasicoherent sheaf to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec A
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi:Spec A\to X
            and taking the global sections over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi M
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M_\phi
          %p
            Clearly,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi O
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            can be much generalized. For example, rings may be noncommutative or one can take category opposite to the category of monads in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            and an arbitrary (not identity) presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            of monads in
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is an example where commutative algebraic monads are used; the theory of quasicoherent sheaves of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
          %h3#AsCocycles As homs into the stack of modules
          %p The above definition may be further re-interpreted as follows.
          .un_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Aff
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi CRing
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff = CRing^{op}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo :
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC : CRing \to Cat
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi S
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mi op
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi f
                        %mo −
                    %mi S
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Spec S \stackrel{f^{op}}{\to} Spec R)
                    \\mapsto (R Mod \stackrel{S \otimes_{f} -}{\to} S Mod)
            %p
              be the (pseudo)functor (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"}> stack
              ) corresponding to the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
              of
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mod
                      %mo →
                      %mi CRing
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod \to CRing
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
              through the 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi CRing
                      %mi op
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y : CRing^{op} \hookrightarrow [CRing,Cat]
              is given on a presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : CRing \to Set
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Ran
                      %mi Y
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    QC(X) := (Ran_Y QC)(X) := [CRing,Cat](X,QC)
                    \\,.
            %p
              When
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is the functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
              by a scheme, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
              is the category of quasicoherent sheaves on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p We now explain the above statement in detail and thereby prove it.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ring"} Ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {}^{op}
            be the category of (commutative, unital)
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            for it regarded as an object of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi op
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi Spec
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec f = f^{op} : Spec(S) \to Spec(R)
            for the morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}
            corresponding to the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : R \to S
            of commutative rings.
          %p
            Consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of (pre)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"}> stack
            s on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo :
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ring
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : Mod \to Ring
            of the category of modules over all rings is the bifibration whose fibered part corresponds to the (pre)stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC \in [C^{op},Cat]
            given on objects by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC : Spec R \mapsto R Mod
          %p and on morphisms by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi S
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mi op
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi f
                  %mi S
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC : (Spec S \stackrel{f^{op}}{\to} Spec R)
                  \\mapsto
                  (R Mod \stackrel{S\otimes_{f} }{\to} S Mod)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where on the right we have the functor that sends any
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            with the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S = {}_S S_R
            with its canonical left
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p One may think of this as the stack of generalized algebraic vector bundles:
          %p
            the operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi f
                  %mo −
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mi Mod
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \otimes_{f} - : R Mod \to S Mod
            corresponds to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle"} bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
            at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
            for more on this.)
          %p
            We may
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} right Kan extend
            the 2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC : CRing^{op} \to Cat
            through the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi CRing
                    %mi op
                  %mo ↪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CRing^{op} \hookrightarrow [CRing,Cat]
            to get a definition of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC
            on arbitrary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi CRing
                            %mi op
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi QC
                        %mtd
                          %mi Cat
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi Ran
                                  %mi Y
                                %mi QC
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi CRing
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Cat
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  CRing^{op} &amp;\stackrel{QC}{\to}&amp; Cat
                  \\\
                  {}^{Y}\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{Ran_Y QC}}
                  \\\
                  [CRing,Cat]
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            Consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in [C^{op},Set]
            any (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"}> pre
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC
            it may be much more generally any presheaf.
          %p
            By the general formula for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            in terms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            given by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi Y
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ring
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi QC
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Ran_Y QC : X \mapsto \int_{R \in Ring} ([Ring,Cat]^{op}(X,Y(R)))^{QC(R)}
          %p
            which using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi CRing
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi CRing
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots = \int_{R \in CRing} [CRing,Cat](X(R), QC(R))
                  \\,.
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "-formula" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^{op},Cat]
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and the 2-functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC
          %p We write for short
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Ran
                    %mi Y
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC(X) := (Ran_Y QC)(X) := [C^{op},Cat](X,QC)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This definition of “generalized vector bundles” on arbitrary presheaves is entirely analogous to the definition of differential forms on arbitrary presheaves, that is discussed in some detail for instance in the entry on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p
            We claim that the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X)
            is the category of quasicoherent sheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as defined by other means above, whenever that other definition applies to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            To see this, straightforwardly unwrap the definition: an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC(X) = [C^{op},Cat](X,QC)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfor"} pseudonatural transformation
            of 2-functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi QC
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : X \to QC
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is regarded as a 2-functor by the canonical embedding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi disc
                  %mo :
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} disc : Set \hookrightarrow Cat
            that regards a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+category"} discrete category
          %p
            The components of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            are
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for each
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi R
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ring
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R \in Ring^{op}
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mrow
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi R
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi QC
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi R
                        %mi Mod
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N|_{Spec R} : X(R) \to QC(R) = R Mod
              %p
                this functor picks one
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi R
                      %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(r) \in R Mod
                for each plot
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi r
                        %mo :
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi R
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Spec
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r : Spec R \to X) \in X(Spec R)
            %li
              %p
                for each morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi Spec
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : Spec A \to Spec B
                a pseudonaturality square
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mi X
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtd
                              %mi X
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi N
                                    %msub
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi Spec
                                        %mi B
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Γ
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo ⇙
                                %mo ≃
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi N
                                    %msub
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi Spec
                                        %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi B
                              %mi Mod
                            %mtd
                              %munder
                                %mo →
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %msub
                                    %mo ⊗
                                    %mrow
                                      %msup
                                        %mi f
                                        %mo *
                                  %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                              %mi Mod
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      X(Spec B)
                      \&amp;\stackrel{X(f)}{\to}&amp;
                      X(Spec A)
                      \\\
                      {}^{\mathllap{N|_{Spec B}}}\downarrow
                      \&amp;{}^{\Gamma(f)}\swArrow_{\simeq}&amp;
                      \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{N|_{Spec A}}}
                      \\\
                      B Mod &amp;\underset{- \otimes_{f^*} A}{\to}&amp; A Mod
                      }
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                (these are subject to coherence conditions). This unwraps to the following data:
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    the component functors
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mrow
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N|_{Spec A}
                    provide an assignment
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ↦
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto N(a)
                    of modules
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(a)
                    to each plot
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo :
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi A
                            %mo →
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi Spec
                            %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a : Spec A \to X) \in X(Spec A)
                %li
                  %p
                    these assignments form a presheaf on the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overcategory"} overcategory
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Aff
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
                    by taking the restriction morphism
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo :
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo →
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          N(f) : N(b) \to N(a)
                  %p to be that underlying the components of the natural isomorphism in the above diagram
                  .maruku-equation
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi b
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi f
                                %mo *
                          %mi A
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo ≃
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          N(b)\otimes_{f^*} A \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} N(a)
                          \\,,
                  %p
                    i.e. the restriction of this morphism to
                    = succeed "." do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,1)
            %li
              %p for each tuple of composable morphisms
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi B
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mrow
                                %mi f
                              %mo ↗
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mo ↘
                                %mi g
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mi Spec
                              %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      \&amp;&amp; Spec B
                      \\\
                      \&amp; {}^f\nearrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^g
                      \\\
                      Spec A &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; Spec C
                      }
              %p
                a pseudo-naturality prism equation relating,
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(f)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(g)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(g\circ g)
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+cohomology"} group cohomology
          %p
            This way, the transformation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : X \to QC
            defines manifestly a quasicoherent sheaf on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Aff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Aff/X
            in the sense of the definition in the above section
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AsSheaves"} As sheaves on Aff/X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi QC
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N : X \to QC
            under this prescription.
          %h3#AsFibHoms As cartesian morphisms of fibrations
          %p
            By the equivalence between
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring \to Cat
            and
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to Ring^{op}
            induced by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
          %p
            Recall from the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            that the equivalence in question is between the following two
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategories
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                on the one hand the bicategory whose objects are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctors"} pseudofunctors
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ring
                        %mo →
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring \to Cat
            %li
              %p
                on the other hand the bicategory whose objects are
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Ring
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to Ring^{op}
                %strong cartesian functors
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi F
                                %mn 1
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo →
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi F
                                %mn 2
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↘
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %mo ↙
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi Ring
                                %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\array{
                      F_1 &amp;&amp;\to&amp;&amp; F_2
                      \\\
                      \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                      \\\
                      \&amp;&amp; Ring^{op}
                      }
              %p
                and whose 2-morphisms are
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
          %p
            Recall furthermore that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : Ring \to Cat
            an ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring \to Set
            via the inclusion
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set \to Cat
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            associated with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+elements"} category of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{op}/X
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Recall furthermore that by definition, the pseudofunctor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ring
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC : Ring Cat
            is the one corresponding to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Mod
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mod^{op} \to Ring^{op}
          %p
            Therefore, by the above equivalence of 2-categories, we find that the category of functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [Ring,Cat](X,QC)
            is equivalent to the category of cartesian functors over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ring
                      %mi Op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ring^{Op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi CartFunc
                    %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartFunc_E(Ring^{op}/X,Mod^{op})
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Ring
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QX
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi CartFunc
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ring
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Mod
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC(X) \simeq [Ring,Cat](X,QX) \simeq CartFunc(Ring^{op}/X, Mod^{op})
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this form quasicoherent sheaves on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are conceived for instance in paragraph 1.1.5 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
              %em Noncommutative stacks
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2333"}> ps
              )
          %p
            Here, as in the above discussion, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            of modules can be replaced by a more general fibered category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi: \mathcal{F}\to\mathcal{B}
            %strong category of quasicoherent modules in
            this
            %strong fibered category
            is the category opposite to the category of cartesian sections of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2305"} dvi
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2333"} ps
          %p
            Given a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Aff}
            of affine schemes (opposite to the category of rings) equipped with some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+coverage"} subcanonical pretopology
            one considers the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi O
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Aff}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Qcoh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Qcoh(\mathrm{Spec}\,R)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Qcoh
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Qcoh
            on an ind-scheme. On ind-schemes Beilinson and Drinfel’d in
          %ul
            %li
              A. Beilinson, V. Drinfel’d,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Hitchin’s integrable system and Hecke eigensheaves on Hitchin system
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~mitya/langlands/hitchin/BD-hitchin.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            consider two variants: a less important variant of quasicoherent
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X^p
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi O
