                      %mo !
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O^!_X
          %h3#Higher Quasicoherent modules in higher/derived geometry
          %p
            The last definition has a straightforward generalization to various
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            setups, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+schemes"} derived schemes
            and other
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+schemes"} generalized schemes
          %h4#by_maps_into_the_stack_
            By maps into the stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QCoh
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QCoh
          %p
            For instance the notion of quasicoherent sheaves generalized to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived stack
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+ring"} simplicial ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+%E2%88%9E-function+theory"} geometric ∞-function theory
            is obtained, we claim, simply by taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %mi SRing
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC : SRing \to (\infty,1)Cat
            to be the functor that assigns the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            for modules over a simplicial ring to any simplicial ring, and then setting for any derived stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QC(X) := Hom(X,QC)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, using the theorem described at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifibration"} bifibration
            of modules over simplicial rings is nothing but the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SRing
          %p
            for any presentable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            whatsoever, we have the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_C \to C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
            classifying it denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QC
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QC : C^{op} \to (\infty,1)Cat
            we may adopt for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo →
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X : C^{op} \to \infty Grpd
            the definition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QX
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi QC
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  QX(X) := [C^{op},(\infty,1)Cat](X,QC)
          %p
            as a definition of generalized
            = succeed "-vector" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-vector+bundle"} ∞-vector bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+%E2%88%9E-stack"} quasicoherent ∞-stack
          %h4#HigherGeometryAsExtensionsOfStructureSheaf As extensions of the structure sheaf
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#LurieQC"}> LurieQC, section 2.2, section 2.3
            ) the following definition is given.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometry (for structured (∞,1)-toposes)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mi mod
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mi op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi cpt
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{G}^{mod} \coloneqq (T (\mathcal{G}^{op}))_{cpt}^{op}
          %p
            be the opposite of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+sub-%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} full sub-(∞,1)-category
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+objects"} compact objects
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} tangent (∞,1)-category
            of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} opposite (∞,1)-category
          %p
            For instance for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+geometry"} E-∞ geometry
            we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi CRing
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G} = CRing_\infty
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+rings"} E-∞ rings
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+morphisms"} etale morphisms
            as admissible maps.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LurieQC"}> LurieQC, above Notation 2.2.4
            )
          %p
            Then the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝒢
                    %mi mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{G} \longrightarrow \mathcal{G}^{mod}
          %p
            is a morphism of discrete
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+%28for+structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes%29"} geometries
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
            an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functor"} left exact (∞,1)-functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi 𝒢
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒳
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{O} \colon \mathcal{G} \longrightarrow \mathcal{X}
          %p
            constitutes a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            and makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{X}, \mathcal{O})
            be a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒢
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{G}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structured+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} structured (∞,1)-topos
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒢
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi 𝒪
                        %mtd
                          %mi 𝒳
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↗
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi 𝒪
                                %mo ,
                                %mi ℱ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒢
                            %mi mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathcal{G} &amp;\stackrel{\mathcal{O}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathcal{X}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{(\mathcal{O}, \mathcal{F})}}
                  \\\
                  \\mathcal{G}^{mod}
                  }
          %p
            exhibits a sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒳
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{X}
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LurieQC"}> LurieQC, notation 2.2.4
            )
          %p
            Now if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{X},\mathcal{O})
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+representable+structured+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} locally representable structured (infinity,1)-topos
            then such an
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℱ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{F}
            is
            %em quasi-coherent
            if also
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒳
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℱ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{X}, (\mathcal{O}, \mathcal{F}))
            is locally representable.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#LurieQC"}> LurieQC, def. 2.3.6
            )
          %h3#SyntheticDescription Synthetic definition using the internal language
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/big+Zariski+topos"} big Zariski topos
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the topos of sheaves over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sch
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sch/X
            (or, more precisely, the affine schemes over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            which are locally of finite presentation). In this topos, there is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
            = succeed "-scheme" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_T(T)
          %p
            A sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of modules over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
            is quasicoherent if and only if, from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+language"} internal point of view
            of the big Zariski topos, the canonical map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \otimes_{\mathbb{A}^1} A \longrightarrow Hom(Hom_{\mathbb{A}^1-Alg}(A, \mathbb{A}^1), N)
          %p
            is bijective for all finitely presented
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathbb{A}^1-Alg}(A, \mathbb{A}^1)
            to the (underlying set of)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
          %p
            This characterization has a geometric interpretation. The set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathbb{A}^1-Alg}(A, \mathbb{A}^1)
            deserves the name “spectrum of
            = succeed "\u201D," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-)rational" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔸
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^1
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is induced from a sheaf of
            = succeed "-modules," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+points"} functor of points
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+spectrum"} relative spectrum
            of that sheaf.
          %p
            The set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔸
                        %mn 1
                      %mo −
                      %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(Hom_{\mathbb{A}^1-Alg}(A, \mathbb{A}^1), N)
            is therefore the set of all
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
