            gives rise to such a function: associate to a pure tensor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \otimes f
            the function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi φ
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi \mapsto f(\varphi) x
          %p
            In a
            = succeed "/algebraic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#quasicoherent_sheaves_over_affine_schemes Quasicoherent sheaves over affine schemes
          %p
            Given an affine scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=\mathrm{Spec}\,R
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a commutative unital ring), the affine Serre theorem establishes the equivalence of the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Qcoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Spec
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Qcoh(\mathrm{Spec}\,R)
            of quasicoherent sheaves (in Zariski topology) and the category of
            = succeed "-modules." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Proj
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Proj(A)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a nonnegatively graded ring, the (projective) Serre theorem establishes the equivalence of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Qcoh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Proj
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Qcoh(\mathrm{Proj}\,(A))
            and the localization of the category of graded
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
          %h3#the_category_of_quasicoherent_sheaves The category of quasicoherent sheaves
          %p
            In the case of general (commutative) schemes, every presheaf of
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi O
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicompact"} quasicompact
            quasiseparated scheme is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+category"} Grothendieck category
            and in particular has enough
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+object"} injective object
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %h3#general General
          %ul
